---
/**
 * Terms of Service, live, customer-facing.
 *
 * Source of truth for the terms text. Ported from the legacy
 * website/terms.html (git bf10a17) and updated for the Lattice rebrand
 * and all three billing channels (Apple App Store IAP, Google Play
 * Billing, Stripe web checkout).
 *
 * Linked from:
 *   - the iOS app purchase flow (PaywallView "Terms of Use" button) —
 *     REQUIRED functional link for App Store Guideline 3.1.2
 *   - the Android app (Settings → About)
 *   - the website Footer component
 *
 * Any time you change material terms, bump EFFECTIVE_DATE.
 */
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';

const EFFECTIVE_DATE   = '2026-07-09';
const LEGAL_ENTITY     = 'KRYPTOKNIGHTZ LLC';
const REGISTERED_ADDR  = '87-154a Maipalaoa Road, Waianae, HI 96792, USA';
const GOVERNING_LAW    = 'the State of Hawaii, United States of America';
const LEGAL_EMAIL      = 'legal@latticevpn.ai';
const SUPPORT_EMAIL    = 'support@latticevpn.ai';
---
<Layout
  bare
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The rules of using Lattice VPN. Short, plain English."
>
  <article class="pt-32 pb-20 mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
    <header class="text-center mb-12">
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-slate-100 border border-slate-200 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold tracking-wide text-slate-600 mb-6">
        TERMS OF SERVICE
      </span>
      <h1 class="font-display font-extrabold text-4xl md:text-5xl tracking-tight text-slate-900 mb-3">
        Terms of Service
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 font-mono">
        Effective {EFFECTIVE_DATE} · Applies to the Lattice VPN applications and the Lattice VPN service.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 font-mono mt-1">
        Provider: {LEGAL_ENTITY} ("Lattice", "we", "us") · Contact: <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_EMAIL}`} class="text-mint-700 underline">{LEGAL_EMAIL}</a>
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Intro -->
    <section class="soft-card rounded-2xl p-7 mb-10">
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of the Lattice VPN
        applications and service ("the Service"), provided by {LEGAL_ENTITY}.
        By installing or using Lattice VPN, you agree to these Terms. These
        Terms constitute the end user license agreement (EULA) for the
        Lattice VPN applications.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 1 -->
    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl text-slate-900 mb-3">1. Description of service</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        Lattice VPN is a virtual private network service that routes your
        internet traffic through one of our region servers using the
        WireGuard protocol with Rosenpass post-quantum key exchange. The
        Service is provided "as is" and "as available."
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 2 -->
    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl text-slate-900 mb-3">2. Eligibility</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        You must be at least 18 years old or have parental consent to use
        the Service. You are solely responsible for any use of the Service
        made under your account.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 3 -->
    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl text-slate-900 mb-3">3. Subscriptions and billing</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        Lattice VPN offers Basic and Pro subscription tiers, each available
        as a monthly or yearly auto-renewing subscription. Your tier
        determines the number of devices you may connect simultaneously.
        Depending on where you subscribe, billing is handled by one of the
        following:
      </p>
      <ul class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed space-y-3 list-disc pl-6">
        <li>
          <strong class="font-semibold">Apple App Store (in-app purchase).</strong>
          Payment is charged to your Apple Account at confirmation of
          purchase. Subscriptions renew automatically for the same price
          and duration unless cancelled at least 24 hours before the end of
          the current period. You can manage and cancel your subscription
          in your Apple Account's Subscriptions settings. Refunds are
          handled by Apple under Apple's standard refund policy.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="font-semibold">Google Play (in-app billing).</strong>
          Subscriptions renew automatically unless cancelled before the end
          of the current period. You can manage and cancel your
          subscription in the Google Play Store's Subscriptions settings.
          Refunds are handled under Google Play's refund policy.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="font-semibold">latticevpn.ai (Stripe).</strong>
          Subscriptions purchased on our website are processed by Stripe
          and renew automatically until cancelled. You can manage and
          cancel your subscription from the account page at
          latticevpn.ai/account.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 4 -->
    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl text-slate-900 mb-3">4. Account number</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        Lattice VPN does not use email addresses or passwords. When you
        subscribe, we generate a random account number, which is your only
        credential for the Service. Keep it safe: anyone who has your
        account number can use your subscription, and if you lose it we may
        be unable to recover your account precisely because we store no
        personal information that could identify it as yours.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 5 -->
    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl text-slate-900 mb-3">5. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">You agree not to use the Service to:</p>
      <ul class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed space-y-2 list-disc pl-6">
        <li>violate any applicable law in your jurisdiction or the jurisdiction of the region server you connect to;</li>
        <li>distribute malware, conduct denial-of-service attacks, or scan systems you do not own;</li>
        <li>send unsolicited bulk email (spam) or perform email-related abuse;</li>
        <li>engage in copyright infringement (the Service is not a tool for piracy);</li>
        <li>distribute content involving the sexual exploitation of minors;</li>
        <li>resell, sublicense, or redistribute access to the Service without our written permission.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mt-3">
        We reserve the right to terminate accounts engaging in any of the
        above without notice or refund.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 6 -->
    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl text-slate-900 mb-3">6. No-logs commitment</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        We do not log your browsing activity, source IP, or DNS queries.
        See our <a href="/privacy" class="text-mint-700 underline">Privacy Policy</a>
        for the complete data handling description.
      </p>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        We will respond to lawful requests for information from competent
        authorities, but cannot produce information we do not collect or
        retain. See our <a href="/canary" class="text-mint-700 underline">warrant canary</a>
        for the latest status on requests received.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 7 -->
    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl text-slate-900 mb-3">7. Service availability</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        We strive for high availability but do not guarantee uninterrupted
        service. Region servers may be taken offline for maintenance,
        software updates, or in response to abuse. We provide multiple
        regions so a single region's unavailability does not prevent
        service use.
      </p>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        We do not guarantee any specific connection speed. Speed depends on
        factors including your local internet connection, the chosen
        region's network conditions, and the destination service's
        responsiveness.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 8 -->
    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl text-slate-900 mb-3">8. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        The Lattice VPN client applications, server software, brand, logo,
        and documentation are owned by {LEGAL_ENTITY} and licensed to you
        for personal use under these Terms. The underlying open-source
        components (WireGuard, Rosenpass, others) are governed by their
        respective licenses.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 9 -->
    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl text-slate-900 mb-3">9. Disclaimers and limitation of liability</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED ON AN "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE" BASIS
        WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING
        WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, OR
        NON-INFRINGEMENT.
      </p>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, {LEGAL_ENTITY}
        SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, CONSEQUENTIAL,
        SPECIAL, OR EXEMPLARY DAMAGES, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO LOSS OF
        DATA, REVENUE, OR GOODWILL, ARISING FROM YOUR USE OF OR INABILITY
        TO USE THE SERVICE.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 10 -->
    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl text-slate-900 mb-3">10. Indemnification</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        You agree to indemnify and hold harmless {LEGAL_ENTITY} from any
        claims, damages, losses, or expenses arising from your violation of
        these Terms or your misuse of the Service.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 11 -->
    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl text-slate-900 mb-3">11. Changes to these Terms</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        We may update these Terms from time to time. Material changes will
        be posted at this URL with an updated effective date. Continued use
        of the Service after a change constitutes acceptance of the updated
        Terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 12 -->
    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl text-slate-900 mb-3">12. Termination</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        You may terminate these Terms at any time by uninstalling the
        applications and cancelling any active subscription. We may
        terminate or suspend your access to the Service at any time for
        violation of these Terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 13 -->
    <section class="mb-10">
      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl text-slate-900 mb-3">13. Governing law</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        These Terms are governed by the laws of {GOVERNING_LAW}, without
        regard to its conflict of law provisions. Any dispute arising under
        these Terms will be resolved in the state or federal courts located
        in Honolulu, Hawaii.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Contact -->
    <section class="soft-card rounded-2xl p-7">
      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl text-slate-900 mb-3">14. Contact</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        Questions about these Terms:
        <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL_EMAIL}`} class="text-mint-700 underline">{LEGAL_EMAIL}</a>
      </p>
      <p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
        General support:
        <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`} class="text-mint-700 underline">{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 font-mono">
        {LEGAL_ENTITY}<br/>
        {REGISTERED_ADDR}<br/>
        Governing law: {GOVERNING_LAW}
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 mt-4">
        See also: <a href="/privacy" class="text-mint-700 underline">Privacy Policy</a> ·
        <a href="/canary" class="text-mint-700 underline">Warrant Canary</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
